WEBVTT

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.350
I'm heading out, Hifumi-chan.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.060
I won't be back to the office today,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.980
so could you show her around, please?

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.540
O-Okay...

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.990
W-Well...

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.650
Please follow me.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.530
Okay.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.990
What sort of restaurant should we pick?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:24.120
<b>Today, at 6:30 PM

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:24.120
<b>Meow</b>

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:24.120
A welcome party for the newbies, huh?

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.570
Welcome, farewell, and year-end parties...

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:29.790
Planning these events is 
a huge responsibility,

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.380
and they say the results 
will affect your reputation.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.630
If we do a bad job...

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.970
We'll be considered completely 
out of touch from now on.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.890
But we can't do too good a job, either.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.520
Huh? Why is that?

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.570
Because we'll get stuck being 
the event planners forever.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.020
We've got our work cut out for us.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.620
<b>French food
Italian
Pizza</b>

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.620
<b>Korean BBQ!
Shabu shabu!
Steak!
Seafood!
Hot pot!
Horse meat!</b>

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.620
<b>Okonomiyaki
A Hamburg steak place
Monja
Sushi</b>

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.070
It can't be <i>too</i> good... This is difficult.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.790
So nothing to complain about, 
but not too memorable, either?

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:33.930
But wouldn't that just make us 
forgettable employees?

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.550
Wouldn't it be better to be an out-of-touch 
employee than a forgettable one?

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.130
Y-Yeah, that wouldn't be a sweet gig.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.630
What are we, comedians?

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.930
So what if we're stuck event 
planning a few times a year?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.810
Why don't we just pick a good place 
that'll make everyone happy?

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.670
Plus, if we pull this off well,

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.070
we'll look more competent in general.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.940
We have nothing to lose by trying our best.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.050
Wh-What?

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.700
It's just, you've sure 
been positive lately, Yun.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.440
Yeah!

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.950
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.170
Aoba-chan, where would you prefer?

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:12.130
Huh? Well, I think a Hamb—

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.170
<i>Oh, no.</i>

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.440
<i>This is a company welcome party. 
I need to pick a restaurant for adults.</i>

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.060
<i>Adults... Adults...</i>

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.260
<i>Alcohol?</i>

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.700
Anywhere that serves great alcohol!

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.640
Um, both you and Mochizuki-san are underage.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:34.090
Huh? Mozuku?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.150
There you are, Mozuku.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.180
Oh, Hazuki-san.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.900
I hear you three are in charge 
of planning the welcome party.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.630
How goes the restaurant selection?

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:50.410
Actually, we're having a 
difficult time deciding.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.790
Do you know of any good places?

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.290
A maid café!

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.230
Huh?

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.300
I'm telling you, I want a maid café.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.100
<i>Yeah, she's definitely a lost cause.</i>

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.740
B-But I've never been to a maid café 
before, and don't know what it's like.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.800
Same here.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.520
Then there's only one thing to do.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:18.190
U-Um, Hazuki-san... What is this?

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.220
Wh-Why do you have <i>these</i> at work?

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.270
It's so airy down there...

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:27.620
Yes, excellent! Just as I 
thought, you're adorable!

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:31.380
Now then, let's act it out 
so you can experience it.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.040
I'll be the customer. You three 
read the lines on this paper.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.610
Huh? Wait, uh...

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.780
Hurry up and open the door.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:44.930
We're starting from there?!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.180
Clack.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:48.870
Stare.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.180
Uh, um...

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.190
W-Welcome home, Miss. 
W-We missed you, meow!

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.060
So sorry. I've been so busy with work.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.900
What would you recommend today?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:06.700
Really? Y-You can't even 
choose for yourself... stupid?

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.620
Oh, fine. I'll choose for you!

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.620
Please do.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:17.860
Here you go. Lemon tea.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.880
Oh, one second, meow.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:25.500
Become delicious. Become delicious!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.270
Okay, here you go.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.380
That's not right.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:29.800
Huh?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.560
You're missing something.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.140
Huh? Do I really have to say that?

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.610
Yup.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.390
O-Okay...

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.510
Moe... moe... kyun!

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.900
<i>What a difficult job!</i>

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:48.910
So... do I not have a character type to play?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.060
It just said to stand here with my tray.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:54.320
Shinoda-kun, you're cute enough 
just standing there quietly.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.940
Use that asset!

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:56.650
Huh?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.090
<i>Grr...</i>

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:08.840
And finally, this is the cafeteria... Huh?!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.060
Oh? Perfect timing.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.430
Why don't you two lovely ladies join us?

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:16.730
I'm going to head back...

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.060
Didn't that give you chills?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.980
<i>So that's Hifumi-senpai's 
"I want nothing to do with this" face.</i>

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.420
Oh, w-we were just—

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.830
So you're the newbie, Mochizuki-kun.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.370
Yup. You're a cutie!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.140
Th-This is for our work, you see!

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.180
Y-Yeah!

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.080
Work. Just work!

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:38.460
Work...

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.240
Oh, I know. Since you're 
here, why don't you join in?

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:43.770
I'm sure you'll look great!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.590
I-It's okay! We have it covered.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:50.510
No need to join in if it's too much for you.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:51.890
Too much?

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:54.870
No.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.380
I can do it.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.680
What?!

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.690
Welcome home, Miss.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.910
Good.! Very good!

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:04.980
Yes, just like that!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.820
Yes! Perfect!

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.090
Wh-While we're at it, 
put on these cat ears, too.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:17.290
Then pose cutely like a cat 
and end your sentences with "meow"!

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.040
Like this... meow?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.880
Yes... Perfect!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:29.810
I know. Next, do a double 
"moe moe kyun" with Suzukaze-kun!

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.980
Guess who?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:34.460
Oh? Who could that cute little voice be?

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:37.100
Is it Toyama-kun? Sakura-kun?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.270
It's me.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.130
Are you quite satisfied, Miss?

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.510
Ow, ow, ow! My neck!

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:44.620
Can't breathe—

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:48.230
Man, now I'm tired.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.780
And we learned nothing useful in the end.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.030
What was the point of all this, anyway?

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.530
That's what we'd like to know.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.660
And so you came crying to me.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.170
Just pick a place and be done with it. Yeesh.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:10.010
Eeny, meeny, miny, moe. My mother says 
to pick the very best one, and you are it.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.010
<b>French food
Monja
Hamburg steak place</b>

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:13.210
A Hamburg steak place? Sounds good to me.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.510
What?! You can't decide like that!

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.470
But it's what my mother says.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.690
Did you want Hamburg steaks that badly, Aoba?

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:26.650
But is there even a Hamburg 
steak place nearby?

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:30.900
What about the place you two took me before?

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.480
It did have a proper restaurant atmosphere.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.660
You're still wearing that?!

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.910
What? You don't have to go to 
school while you're interning?

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:46.250
Yes. At our vocational school, 
internships can count for class credit.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.840
Luck you. I have to 
work while going to school.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.760
You must be quite busy.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:58.010
But it's okay! I've totally 
gotten used to coming to work.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.180
It was last summer when you first came, 
wasn't it, Sakura-san?

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:03.870
Last summer?

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.140
I worked here part-time as a debugger.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.970
So that's why you seem at home here,
even though you're a trainee like us.

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:12.870
Then I should call you "Senpai."

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.430
Huh? S-Senpai?

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.450
Aw, you're making me blush.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:22.340
Don't get a big head. You're also 
new as a programmer, Sakura-san.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.080
So you don't need to 
worry about that, Narumi-san.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.130
Then as fellow new programmers,

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:31.900
let's both do our best to get 
hired full-time in three months.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.130
Sure thing!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:38.010
Though it's getting my contract 
renewed, in my case.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.830
Oh, and no need to be so polite. 
You can call me by my given name.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.100
In that case, people usually call me Naru.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.310
Narucchi it is! Nice to meet you.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.710
You, too, Nenecchi.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.490
I hear the food here's great!

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:52.060
<i>Looks like things are going well over there.</i>

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.060
Have you been here before?

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:52.770
Nope!

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:15.180
D-Do you have a nickname people 
often call you, Mochizuki-san?

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.510
Naru always calls me Momo.

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:24.940
"Momo" for Mochizuki Momiji, huh? 
Then we'll call you Momo-chan.

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.890
Feel free to loosen up and 
call us by our given names, too.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:31.390
Um, then...

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.400
<i>She's looking at something?</i>

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.900
Aoba-san, Yun-san, Hajime-san,

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.530
and Leader Hifumi.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.780
L-Leader?

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:44.210
You're not wrong, but that's 
the first I've heard that used.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:44.210
Leader... Leader...

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.730
Oh, while we're on 
the subject, Hifumi-senpai...

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:52.300
You call Yagami-san and Toyama-san 
by their given names with "-chan,"

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.790
despite their seniority.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:58.980
Oh, I used to ask her to be 
my conversation practice partner,

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:00.390
so I made her call me that.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.830
Yeah... And it stuck.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.010
Then what about Toyama-san?

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.660
Once I started using "Ko-chan",

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.570
one day, Rin-chan told me to 
refer to her that way, too.

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.940
Oh, really? I wonder why.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:16.440
I-I think she just didn't 
want to be left out.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.820
Huh? What do you mean?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.320
A complicated feeling, indeed.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:27.170
Are you all right? The cast 
auditions are just beginning.

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.870
Yes. Someone must be talking about me.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:35.320
That's right! You rarely get a 
chance to meet so many cute girls!

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.970
Ooh, she's cute, too.

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.010
Just don't choose by appearance.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.010
Here are your orders.

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.430
You ordered extra pasta?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.620
You must eat quite a bit.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:47.430
Yes.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:52.020
So lucky... And yet you 
have like the perfect body.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:55.420
Whenever I eat, it immediately shows.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:58.480
Wh-What?

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.490
But you're not fat, 
and I think you're cute.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.100
Huh?

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.110
Well aren't you such a sweet, 
honest girl, Momo-chan!

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:09.700
Here, have some of this!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.250
<i>That didn't take much.</i>

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.500
Thank you for coming!

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:16.420
Do you live at your parents' place, Narucchi?

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:18.750
No, I room with Momo.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:23.380
<i>I'm really not good with stuff like this.</i>

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:28.820
Iijima Yun-san, Shinoda Hajime-san, 
Takimoto Hifumi-san,

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:33.310
Ahagon Umiko-san, 
Sakura Nene-san, Suzukaze Ao...

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.560
You wrote down all our names?

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:41.820
I-Is there a problem with that? 
I don't want to mess anyone's up again.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.820
I'm not good with remembering them.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.700
No, it's fine.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:51.830
I think it's admirable to try and 
remember so many names at once.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.750
<i>Suzukaze Aoba...</i>

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.940
Lunch time!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.650
Where should we go, Aoba-chan?

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:14.800
I was thinking about buying a premade lunch.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.270
I'll probably do that, too.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.810
So, Momo-chan, I suppose as usual...

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:23.860
The size of your rice balls 
never fails to amaze me.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:29.270
I was so surprised when I first saw one, 
but I'm starting to get used to it.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.330
Good on you for bringing your 
own lunch every day, Momo-chan.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.920
Why don't you come to the 
cafeteria to eat with us?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:42.190
No thank you. I feel more relaxed here.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.550
Unless...

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.420
Unless?

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:48.240
Is there something you can only 
discuss with me at the cafeteria?

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.180
No, nothing like that...

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:54.810
You can't seem to break the ice with Momiji?

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:58.950
Yes. It's like we're 
on different wavelengths.

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.010
Like her guard's up around me.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:03.860
It must be love!

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.190
I'm trying to have a serious conversation!

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.200
But if she <i>were</i> in love with me...

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.260
at least it'd be a straightforward choice 
of accepting or turning her down.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:17.210
<b>Munch Munch Munch</b>

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.210
It's oddly amusing, the levity 
with which you just said that.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:21.540
What do you think of Momiji, Aoba?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.240
Me?

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:27.550
She's responsible and nice, 
but she seems a bit standoffish.

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:31.180
Sounds just like Yagami 
when she first started.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.170
Gah! Hazuki-san.

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.260
Really?

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:37.430
So Momo-chan will 
someday go around in panties?!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.650
Is that the only thing you 
associate with me, Aoba?!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:44.980
Momo-chan cares about how she dresses, 
so I doubt that'll happen.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.440
Way to take a jab at Yagami-san.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:50.950
You never know. 
She might actually be a regular slob.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:54.780
You should see the way I sprawl out at home.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.450
Er, that's honestly pretty easy to imagine.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.060
Huh? No way!

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.710
We've been together constantly 
at work for over a year.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.970
Together constantly...

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:10.220
I... don't know anything about Momo-chan.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.850
That has to change, no doubt about it!

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.560
So, um... Hajime-san! Yun-san!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:34.100
Momo-chan...

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.890
Um, uh...

00:15:36.890 --> 00:15:38.720
Is your rice ball good?

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:39.690
Yes.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.960
You can't have any.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.500
No... That wasn't my intention.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:51.650
So you don't... go to the 
cafeteria... for lunch either...

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:54.820
You don't go often either, Hifumi-senpai.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:59.060
Right. It's because Sojiro... 
Oh, he's my pet...

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.750
I like to eat breakfast with him...

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.370
But I get why the cafeteria 
might wear you out.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:10.940
Interacting with others 
is difficult, isn't it?

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:16.090
Not really. I feel like I'm doing 
everything that's needed of me.

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:17.490
As for studying,

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:20.700
I've completed each day's 
assigned chapters on time.

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:24.510
Is there something that I'm not doing right?

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.870
No, not at all.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:31.270
You have experience with 3D, so I think 
you'll be able to start work soon.

00:16:31.270 --> 00:16:34.140
Probably even sooner than Aoba-chan did...

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:39.310
But I'm sort of more worried about you
than I was about Aoba-chan...

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:40.350
Worried?

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.980
No! I'm sorry!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:46.540
Um... Um... Um...

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.010
O-Oh yeah!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.950
Do you want to see Sojiro?

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.230
Your pet?

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:52.430
Here.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:53.740
Oh, a hedgehog.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.110
He's cute.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.420
<b>Beware of heat exhaustion!</b>

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.420
<b>Make sure you're
eating properly.</b>

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.420
<b>Meow</b>

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:05.420
I'm back.

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:08.340
Oh, what are you looking at?

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:11.180
Hifumi-senpai was showing me her pet.

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:14.080
So this is the famous Sojiro-kun.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.180
He's cute.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:19.180
You're becoming more and more 
of a leader, Hifumi-chan.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.330
Oh... No, not at all...

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.030
<i>Was she trying to be considerate of me?</i>

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:40.380
I'm home.

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:41.610
Welcome back.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.410
I got back first, so I'm making dinner.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.090
Thanks. What are we eating tonight?

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:52.920
Ta-da!

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.820
A full course of bean sprouts!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.850
How's it going with the character team?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.350
Normal. How about you?

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.540
I think things are going pretty well.

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:12.140
Umiko-san's a bit scary, 
but Nenecchi's a lot of fun.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.110
Naru.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.610
About tomorrow's lunch...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.230
Lunch time!

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:30.610
Ta-da! Today, I made some rice balls!

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.720
No way! You, too, Aoba-chan?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:36.430
What a coincidence! Same here.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:38.080
Nice acting.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.970
I made some sandwiches.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.050
Momo-chan, do you have your usual...

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:51.610
I thought I'd also 
go buy some lunch today.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.890
But you still have a rice ball.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:57.570
If I buy enough food to make me full, 
I'll run out of money.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.880
Do you live on your own, Momo-chan?

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:03.950
No, I live with Naru. 
We moved to Tokyo together.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:09.110
Yeah, I totally get that. When you 
have to pay rent, your money just...

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:11.380
You've also got all 
the toys you buy to blame.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.680
Y-You think so?

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:14.960
That never occurred to you?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.090
<b>Everyone, do your best!!</b>

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.090
<b>Yeah!!</b>

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.090
Huh? Of course it did!

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:20.770
I want to hurry up, make a lot 
of money, and eat a lot of meat.

00:19:20.770 --> 00:19:22.490
Be mindful of your weight.

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:24.580
So where are you from?

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.740
Hokkaido.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:26.960
Really?

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:31.910
Our office trip last year was to Hokkaido. 
The seafood was so good!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.190
It is, isn't it?

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:36.170
The seafood in Tokyo just isn't the same.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.690
Plus, it's expensive.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.420
Why don't we go buy some side dishes?

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:47.070
We need something 
to go with our rice balls, too.

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:47.950
Yeah.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.460
Come on. Let's go!

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.080
Momo-chan!

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:58.170
Today, I'll introduce you to 
the master of Eagle Jump, Mozuku—

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:01.420
Huh?

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.750
Have you gotten used to coming to the office?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:07.600
Yes.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:11.560
I see. The morning rush 
is pretty rough, isn't it?

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:13.970
Um, Aoba-san.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.100
Yes?

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:18.690
I'm the newbie here, so you don't 
have to talk to me so formally.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.970
Oh, please excuse—I mean, sorry.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:24.200
You're right. I'm just not used to it.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.090
Momo... Is it okay if I call you Momiji-chan?

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:31.510
We have that connection 
with our names' meanings.

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:35.460
We're the same age, so you don't 
have to speak to me formally, either.

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.930
I have to. You've worked here
over a year longer than I have.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:43.630
You're pretty by-the-book, Momiji-chan.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:47.010
Aoba-san, seeing as we're the same age,

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:50.270
are you not at all 
concerned about my skill level?

00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.580
Or as a character designer, 
are you above it all?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.520
Huh?

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:02.740
I was number one in my 
class, so I'm pretty good.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.610
I should be.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:06.410
Of course I'm concerned.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:08.260
You are?

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.220
O-Oh really? I see.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.700
And that's why...

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:15.540
I won't lose, either.

00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:22.280
<i>How can she say that while 
looking so positive?</i>

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:26.930
<i>I don't get it. Her desire not to lose 
is somehow different from mine.</i>

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:31.140
<i>Darn it. Being around Suzukaze 
Aoba throws me off.</i>

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.180
<i>What is this feeling?</i>

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:36.440
If you don't hurry, we'll leave you behind.

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:42.440
<i>Suzukaze Aoba... I won't lose, either.</i>

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:47.450
Well, please do your best today, too...

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:48.460
Okay.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.370
These variant designs... 
Did Aoba-san draw them?

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:59.260
Yeah, she did. Aren't they cute?

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:03.500
Eh? Huh?

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.470
You really are good... Suzukaze Aoba.
